{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"New Jersey security deposit maximum and annual increase cap","requirement":"A landlord may not collect a security deposit above one and one-half times one month's rent, may not raise it more than 10% a year, and at the start of a lease may require no more than the deposit plus the first month's rent.","key_value":"1.5 months' rent; 10% yearly increase cap","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies in New Jersey; a landlord is not required to collect a deposit but must follow the law if one is taken.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential rentals statewide"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2","quoted_span":"The maximum-security deposit to be collected by the landlord cannot be more than one and one-half times one month’s rent ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2 ). It can be less. Any additional yearly security deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit interest and account requirements","requirement":"Security deposit money remains the tenant's property, must be held in trust in a New Jersey insured bank, savings and loan or money market account, and the interest earned belongs to the tenant.","key_value":"Interest to tenant; paid at renewal/anniversary or January 31","coverage_conditions":"Landlords holding security deposits for residential tenancies in New Jersey; account options differ for ten or more units and ten or fewer units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential rentals statewide"},"exemptions":"Security deposits for seasonal use or rental (term of not more than 125 consecutive days for a person with a permanent residence elsewhere).","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19","quoted_span":"The interest or earnings paid on the security deposit belongs to the tenant and shall be paid to the tenant in cash or credited toward rent due and owing on the ren ewal or anniversary of the tenant’s lease or on January 31, if the tenant has been given written notice, that the interest payments will be paid on January 31 of each year","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit notice to tenant and tenant remedy","requirement":"Within 30 days of receiving a deposit, and at each annual interest payment, the landlord must give the tenant written notice of the bank or investment company, the amount, account type and interest rate; if the landlord fails to give notice or pay interest, the tenant may apply the deposit plus 7% interest to rent.","key_value":"30-day notice; 7% per annum","coverage_conditions":"Landlords holding security deposits for residential tenancies in New Jersey.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential rentals statewide"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"After written notice and 30 days to comply, the tenant may apply the deposit and interest to rent; the landlord may then not demand an additional security deposit.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19.1","quoted_span":"Within 30 days of receipt of the security deposit and at t he time of each annual interest payment, the landlord must notify the tenant in writing of the name and address of the banking institution or investment company in which the money is deposited, the amount of the deposit, type of account, and current rate o f interest for the account.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return within 30 days and double damages","requirement":"Within 30 days after a tenancy ends the landlord must return the deposit plus interest, less deductions, and send an itemized list of deductions by registered or certified mail.","key_value":"30 days; double the amount wrongfully withheld","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies in New Jersey; if the tenant broke the lease, the 30 days runs from re-rental or lease expiration, whichever is first.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential rentals statewide"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Tenant may sue for double the amount wrongfully withheld, plus court costs and reasonable attorney’s fees.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1","quoted_span":"Within 30 days after the termination of a tenancy, a landlord must return the security deposit, plus interest earned less deductions, to the tenant ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return after displacement","requirement":"Within five business days after a tenant is displaced by fire, flood, condemnation or evacuation, the landlord must return the security deposit, and within three business days tell the tenant where it can be collected.","key_value":"5 business days","coverage_conditions":"Tenants displaced by fire, flood, condemnation or evacuation from residential rentals in New Jersey.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Displaced residential tenants"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1","quoted_span":"Within five (5) business days after a tenant is displaced by fire, flood, condemnation, or evacuation, the landlord must return the security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return after Safe Housing Act termination","requirement":"When a tenant terminates a lease under the Safe Housing Act, the landlord must make the security deposit plus interest available within 15 business days and within 3 business days notify the tenant in writing where and when to collect it.","key_value":"15 business days","coverage_conditions":"Tenants who end a lease under the New Jersey Safe Housing Act because of domestic violence.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Safe Housing Act lease terminations"},"exemptions":"Does not apply to transient or seasonal rentals.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6","quoted_span":"Within 15 business days after the lease is terminated, the landlord shall make available the return of the tenant’s security deposit, plus any interest earned, to the tenant or the tenant’s agent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
